From 346d352d3cc846bc48d8a75528dba9ceff6b4989 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pongsathon Kheereekaew <kpongsat@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 22:45:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(streaming): optional placeholder message before
 first streamed token
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add `placeholder_text` to the streaming config (default off). When set, the
stream consumer sends a short editable message immediately — before the first
token arrives — so users on slow-first-token models see instant feedback.
The first real delta then edits the placeholder in place (single message, no
spam). Best-effort: a failed placeholder send is swallowed and the normal
first-send path still delivers the answer. Edit transport only (native draft
streaming is already a live preview).

- StreamConsumerConfig.placeholder_text + _send_placeholder() helper
- StreamingConfig.placeholder_text + to_dict/from_dict round-trip
- gateway/run.py wires it through to the consumer config (both call sites)
- 6 new tests (behaviour + config round-trip), 305 regression tests green

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
